From 72a2a671eea99cd4c883a4ecbdcc504b211298f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Redgrave961 <214504937+Redgrave961@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 00:42:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Runtime: invalid calls and DMAs fail loudly; drop workarounds
 and stale hooks

An indirect call to a target that is not lifted code (null, data, or an
unregistered address) and a guest callback whose OPD does not resolve now
stop with a register, descriptor and guest-stack report, as the PPU would
fault; they used to return silently, no-op with r3=0, skip past a recursion
cap or spin until a streak counter tripped, which turned real bugs into
freezes far from their cause. The dispatch path is a lookup and a call; the
per-call env-gated hooks (call trace, ring, cscheck, icall histogram,
TOC watch, another title's probe addresses), the never-registered OPD fixup
table and the vcall/depth bookkeeping are gone.

MFC transfers follow the hardware rules: size 0 completes as a no-op;
misalignment, a reserved or out-of-range EA, or an LS overrun is a fatal
fault rather than a silently dropped transfer. Guest pages commit on first
touch through the VM fault handler, so the per-DMA VirtualQuery check and its
page bitmap are removed. sys_tty_write returns EFAULT for an invalid buffer
instead of clamping the length.
---
